WEBVTT

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.410
<i>In the beginning, God created 
the heavens and the earth.</i>

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.280
<i>He followed them</i>

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.110
<i>with light, waters, and the land.</i>

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:26.790
<i>Then he created the many animals 
that would inhabit it.</i>

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.500
<i>Or... that was the plan.</i>

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.000
<i>It got too tedious, so he outsourced it.</i>

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:39.180
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.510
How did you like my snake fist?

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.500
When did you even learn that?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.270
But I've got something up my sleeve, too!

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.000
What?!

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.500
Hidden Technique: Bone Hug!

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.590
That's dangerous! What's with those bones?!

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.570
They're ribs!

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:51.450
What are they doing?

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.510
No idea.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.680
Yeah, that's a nope.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.170
It's impossible to make bones 
grow that fast on Earth.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.610
Aw, man, and I just got the 
order for "bones as weapons."

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:07.300
I guess this won't do. Oh, well, 
this hurts like heck, anyway.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.920
Why is Jupiter-san modifying himself?

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.100
He was saying that it's easier to 
make something if he's felt it,

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.930
but I think he just wants to play around.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:19.420
If rapid growth is impossible, 
how about having folded ones unfurl?

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.000
Could work.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.550
But you'd get hurt every 
time the bones come out.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.170
If you're wounded often, I don't think
 you'd wind up dead, even if you didn't fight.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.290
I suppose it could work as an 
"emergency sacrificial defense"

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:34.680
for amphibian species that 
can regenerate skin quickly.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.010
I see! I'll jot that down.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.330
Are you all right?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.650
Yes, probably.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.570
I know you want them to 
shoot out like before...

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.940
This is what would be ideal.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:53.040
But if you actually did that, 
the exit wounds would be too big,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.080
<b>Just a little bit</b>

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.710
so you can only extend them a little bit.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.210
<b>Just a little bit</b>

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.810
These aren't what I envisioned.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.850
They're not very impressive, 
and they seem painful.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.900
Having a weapon snikt out from 
your body is indeed awesome.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.850
Yup, yup.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.220
If storing them won't work,
 I at least want them to be flashy!

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.960
Got it! Let's put the 
bones outside the body!

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.480
I've put the spine and the 
ribs outside! How about that?

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.380
Wait, wait! How are you moving those arms?!

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.610
What's the issue?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:28.000
He's not a snake! The shoulder 
blades behind his ribs are missing.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.610
And his arms are supposed 
to be attached to those!

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:34.490
I've flipped the position of the bones.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.800
I went all-out and put the shoulder 
blades inside. Can you see?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:43.010
<b>Shoulder Blade</b>

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:43.010
<b>Rib</b>

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.470
You can move your arms... 
so is this arrangement okay?

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:43.010
What does Mars-san think?

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:47.000
She doesn't seem satisfied, 
but she's not saying no.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.250
Maybe this is viable?

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.020
So that means this direction is okay!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.270
You should check the durability, too.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.380
I brought a lion.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.100
All right, go get those bones!

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.380
Why did you start with an end boss?!

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.670
He's eating them like 
they're bone crackers.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.960
Man, he snapped a bunch 
off right at the base.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.710
The part where they join up is the weakest.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.180
I-Is he okay?

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.570
You can't use them as 
weapons if they've been eaten.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:27.260
Mars-san, is there a way to 
make the joints stronger?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.440
Let's see.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.060
If you're fine with the bones not moving,

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:31.810
<b>Bone</b>

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:31.810
<b>Joint</b>

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:31.810
<b>Bone</b>

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.740
you could offset and double them up.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.680
<b>Double Them Up</b>

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.680
<b>Offset Them</b>

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.320
Oh, that's brittle.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:39.800
So tough!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.030
I see!

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.930
But there's a different downside.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.290
Let's implement that right away!

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:46.950
<b>Doubled-Up Bones</b>

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.930
Bring it on!

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.700
His teeth are no match for 
the reinforced bones!

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.460
But won't that...

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.340
Is that our usual trope again?!

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.700
I knew it.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.660
Difficulty breathing.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.990
Difficulty breathing?

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.720
It's not osteoporosis this time?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.770
It's hard to breathe without ribs.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:13.930
<b>Inhale {purple}</b>

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.250
When you breathe, your chest 
moves up and down, right?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:14.850
<b>Exhale {green}</b>

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:15.680
<b>Inhale {purple}</b>

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:16.640
<b>Exhale {green}</b>

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.600
That's proof that your ribs are moving.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:17.430
<b>Inhale {purple}</b>

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:18.350
<b>Exhale {green}</b>

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.980
The lungs move as they are pulled 
by the ribs and the diaphragm.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.190
<b>Inhale {purple}</b>

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.100
<b>Exhale {green}</b>

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:20.350
<b>Diaphragm</b>

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:20.850
<b>Diaphragm</b>

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:20.940
<b>Inhale {purple}</b>

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:21.980
<b>Diaphragm</b>

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:21.810
<b>Exhale {green}</b>

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.870
I see. They're like bellows.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.870
Someone... help...

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:32.480
Pluto-chan, didn't you make an animal 
that can breathe without ribs?

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.000
You mean the frog!

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.490
Frogs don't have ribs?!

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:40.050
When I made the leg bones tougher 
to withstand big jumps,

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.400
the ribs got in the way, so I removed them!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.250
Then how do they breathe?

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.660
With determination!

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.010
<b>Bam</b>

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:47.370
Determination?

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.480
It's just using determination 
and its throat to breathe.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:52.890
So that state means it's 
super-full of determination.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:56.220
You hear that, Jupiter? 
Just use your determination.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.620
He's been breathing hard this whole time, 
but he's still oxygen deprived.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:05.150
If you breathe without ribs and just 
your throat, you get less oxygen,

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.400
so frogs use cutaneous 
respiration in addition.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.440
Want to turn into an amphibian 
and make your skin slimy?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.020
That's not what I envisioned.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:17.900
What about <i>not</i> using the 
ribs to move the lungs?

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.170
That's it!

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.040
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.390
How about using the shoulder blades 
I moved inside to move the lungs?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.910
<b>Inhale</b>

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:21.790
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.670
<b>Inhale</b>

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.540
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.540
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:24.980
That should be possible.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.420
<b>Inhale</b>

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.420
<b>Inhale</b>

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.290
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.170
I think it'll make your arms move 
around every time you breathe, though.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.170
<b>Inhale</b>

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.050
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:27.920
<b>Inhale</b>

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:28.170
<b>Exhale</b>

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.210
Applying that allowed me to breathe.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.300
Then why are you crawling like that?

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.060
Well, it's really hard to move.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.930
Of course, fast animals

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.310
bend their spines to attain a longer stride.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:46.540
Having an immobile back is 
a bigger issue than I thought.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:49.680
But the organs are protected, 
so it's fine, isn't it?

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.750
All right, I'll make the ribs even longer!

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:57.580
Oh, no, Jupiter-san! Is this...

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.640
Yup, osteoporosis.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.090
I thought so.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.830
You need to reduce your calcium usage.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.050
I don't want to! The ribs are so cool now!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.580
I'd rather save somewhere else.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:14.490
Oh, yeah, the teeth! 
They're veritable chunks of calcium!

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.100
Let's lose the teeth and redistribute 
that calcium to the ribs.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.450
How will you eat?

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:23.240
How about Venus's bird system? 
Grind it up in your stomach.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:28.730
Sounds good. Bird beaks are hardened skin,
 so you barely need any calcium.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.360
Okay, let's go with that.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.520
I have a foundation now,
 so I just need to sketch this.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.870
Aw, my hand moves when I breathe. 
I can't draw like this.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.430
Just go back to normal!

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.610
Oh, right.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.360
A beak instead of teeth!

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.620
Reroute the extra calcium to the bones!

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:48.620
Move the spine and ribs outside the body!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.080
Reinforce the bones by doubling them up!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.300
It'll be hard to move and get food,

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.130
but we'll compensate for that 
with an energy-saving body!

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.010
Swap the position of the ribs 
and the shoulder blades,

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.760
and have the shoulder blades aid breathing!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:08.020
<b>Turtle</b>

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.840
It's done! An animal with amazing ribs!

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.180
God has spoken!

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.650
Accepted!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.020
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:11.020
So its shell is made from ribs?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.370
But isn't the head exposed?

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.960
The shell's pointless if the head gets eaten.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:18.690
I'll think about that now. Any good ideas?

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.760
Turn the neck and stow the head away!

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.020
I like that!

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.330
God has spoken!

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.160
<b>Chelidae</b>

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.840
Accepted!

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.160
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.390
What about one where it folds 
up and retracts the head?

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.830
I like that, too.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.370
God has spoken!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.170
<b>Chinese
 Pond Turtle</b>

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:31.810
Accepted!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.170
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:36.440
It's not quite hidden, though. 
The soft parts are still visible.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.090
You want it to fully hide?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.170
If possible.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:44.180
Then how about adding hinges to the 
belly that make it completely shut?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:41.930
<b>Hinge</b>

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.430
<b>Hinge</b>

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.170
G-God has spoken!

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.190
Accepted!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.190
<b>Asian Box Turtle</b>

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:48.850
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:51.180
Yay, an acceptance frenzy!

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.190
<b>A Few Days Later...</b>

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.400
Jupiter-san, what's that?

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.810
The client said that, 
while the turtle's fine,

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.990
after some thought, it became clear

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.080
that the bones aren't much like weapons.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.000
So then this plain guy I was
 sketching got accepted.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.620
<b>Iberian
 Ribbed Newt</b>

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:08.460
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:08.130
Th-That's good for you.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.960
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.170
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.660
This is the newt that fights by 
poking its ribs out of the body!

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:21.250
See, the ribs open up like this,
 and go through the skin.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.260
The bones having a pointy tip is good design.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.020
It makes it easier for them to pierce the skin.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.530
But does this actually 
have any defensive merit?

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.010
What you didn't know is that 
they are also poisonous!

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:36.360
After they create a wound 
with their bone spikes,

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.060
applying that poison works really well!

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:41.530
An' it hoits when y'try to eat 'em...

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.470
Ow, ow, ow...

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:46.540
Jupiter-san, you totally tried 
to eat that newt, didn't you?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.160
Huh? Huh?

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.410
What's wrong, Shimoda-kun?

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.140
It's dangerous to stand 
in the door like that.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:07.610
I'm sorry! I just came here to see 
how the project is progressing,

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.800
but nobody is here.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.140
How is that "courting that 
causes a throb" request going?

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.330
I think everybody is busy 
behind those doors.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:16.570
I'm excited.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.690
Tugging on the heart strings is 
my forte, so I'm basically done.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.200
Is that yours?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.400
Just its looks alone are adorable!

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:31.200
But the others aren't coming out.
 Maybe they're stuck?

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.510
Shimoda-kun, if you're 
going to make the rounds,

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.920
I can come with you, if you want.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:38.210
Thank you, Neptune-san. That'll be helpful!

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.920
Let's start with this door.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:45.470
Excuse me—

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.240
Lu la la...

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.200
Extending feathers...

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.190
Elongating flesh...

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.450
It's all for love!

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.620
Shining feathers...

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.560
Captivating voices...

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.870
This, too, is love!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.170
Lu la la...

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.530
I am pretty!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.860
My beauty...

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:09.650
It's a skill.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:11.870
It's hard to stay pretty.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.790
Yes, so hard to stay pretty!

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.740
<i>She's enjoying singing that weird song.</i>

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.000
A...ny...way!

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.510
Anyway, it's not free!

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.400
Not free!

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:25.510
She transformed!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:34.410
Since I can afford to maintain 
such beauty, my ability is superior!

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.890
Lu la la...

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:41.280
I am pretty!

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.790
I am...

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.290
Huh? Pretty?

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.950
Lu la la...

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:51.230
I am pretty!

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:55.410
You are pretty...

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.550
M-May I have a word?

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:01.470
What is it? Can't you see I'm 
working so hard on courtship here?

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:04.310
Uh, well, I just wanted to confirm that 
this is indeed your work in progress

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.540
for the "courting that 
causes a throb" request.

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.530
Didn't that cause a heart to throb?!

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.480
When birdies' feathers are beautiful, 
they're saying they're healthy.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:13.890
When they sing well, 
they're saying they're smart.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.560
Their sweet chirp-chirp lyrics
 all basically mean this.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:21.580
I... I see. The only lyric I didn't quite 
get was the "elongating flesh" one?

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:25.850
That's about the birdies that grow 
flesh to transform for love.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:32.910
<b>Temminck's
Tragopan</b>

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:31.480
You know how roosters have flesh that 
hangs from their chin, called a wattle?

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.170
That part can get elongated.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.460
<b>Love Mode</b>

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.460
<b>Wattle</b>

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.450
I see.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.050
How was that? That made your 
heart skip a beat, right?

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:40.520
Uh, well, it was really wonderful, but...

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:41.340
But?

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.510
When it's just you, Ven-chan, 
there's no frame of reference

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:48.590
for me to tell whether you're 
better or worse than any other?

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:53.850
Of course! How could I be so blind?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.060
Shimoda-kun, dance with me!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.390
Copy my moves!

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.300
Here we go.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.860
Lu la la...

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.870
Lu la la...

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.040
And now? I'm better, right?!

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.380
Y-Yes.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:15.370
Intense courting is more 
embarrassing than adorable.

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.680
That's it!

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:21.110
I'll make my bad student come with 
me to show off how good I am.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.820
That's a foolproof courting method.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:27.790
So as your bad student, I'm just 
there to make you look better?

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:28.890
For now!

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:33.680
But the days you spend dancing with me
 will surely pay off at some point.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.380
Shimoda-kun, I want you 
to surpass me one day.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:43.610
And then, if I take on a student...

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:48.520
You are the one to shine next!

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.390
I see! This is the love 
between teacher and student.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.460
That's a nice story.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.400
That really did get to my heart.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:57.650
It's done! A bird that forms a 
dance team with its bad student!

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:59.670
God has spoken!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:03.060
Accepted! Bravo!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:05.550
<b>Long-Tailed
 Manakin</b>

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:05.550
<b>Accepted</b>

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.540
We also got Neptune-san's heart to throb!

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.920
I did it! I'm the first one done!

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.740
Were we able to help?

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.640
Let's go and talk to who's next.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.120
Huh?

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:23.680
It sounds like someone's having a fight.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:28.440
Is that Pluto-san, Mercury-san, 
and Jupiter-san?

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:31.760
Wait, are the two of them 
fighting over Pluto-chan?!

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:32.940
Oh, no!

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.460
Actually, no! It's not a fight,
 more of a... duel?

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.990
Yo! Should we start this, 
and exit the friend zone?

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:41.200
Yo! Should we settle this, 
the principles of our hormones?

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.330
Survival of the fittest is what I represent!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.470
Sadly for you, it's my vocation to present.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.210
It's a rap battle!

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.230
They're trying to judge who's the 
best with a flurry of rhymes!

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:52.750
You seem oddly familiar 
with this sort of thing, Shimoda-kun.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.670
Strength is appetite, gluttony emotion,

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.460
always with a smile, ready to dig in!

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.980
My strength is innovation,

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.400
step to me, I'll make you feast on poison.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.110
I'm the only one, that's my style.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.120
You're the lonely one, 
just a jeering smile.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:06.120
This has no end.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:07.140
But we must defend!

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.140
Who will win? That girl 
decides who gets in!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.750
Interlude...

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.160
You there, do some beatboxing!

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.530
What's "beatboxing"?

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.990
I am noble, you are trouble!

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:25.000
You are cynical, but I am lyrical!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.100
Always hungry, what's your issue?

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:29.010
Always forcin' it, you're stuck in glue.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.990
I'll be the one accepted, you're at a dead end!

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:34.800
Neptune-san, be the judge please.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.400
I can't! I don't know what's 
good or bad in rapping.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:41.380
Besides, isn't that what 
Pluto-chan is here for?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:45.010
I'm sorry, the waterfall was too 
loud for me to hear anything.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:52.390
Does that mean MC Mercury and 
MC Jupiter's efforts were in vain?!

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:56.470
No, not in vain. There's something 
we can learn from this!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:59.520
We were trying to see if Pluto-chan's 
heart would react if we sang her

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.410
a love song in the same 
environment as frogs do.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.710
Frogs? Oh, that's why we're by the water.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:09.580
No matter how hard you try, 
if she can't hear, she can't hear!

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:13.120
Neptune-san's "I don't get it"
 was also helpful.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.050
No matter how sick our rhymes are,

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.420
if the listener doesn't understand,
 what's the point?

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.420
I'm s-sorry...

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:22.300
So why is it rap for frogs?

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:26.200
Frog songs are closer to a rap battle 
than a singing contest.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:32.190
<b>Not Popular</b>

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:32.190
<b>Popular</b>

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:30.690
The frogs' ribbit battle is about who 
can make these low sounds faster.

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:35.030
I wanted to see what it feels like 
to be struck by love as a female frog,

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.370
so I asked these two for help.

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:41.440
That means a rice paddy in the summer 
as the stage for a freestyle rap battle!

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:46.040
If we can't settle this by singing, 
we'll have to resort to physical combat.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.950
The stronger one will be chosen!

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:50.310
Bring it on!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:54.960
They don't have to really fight.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:58.930
You need to show off your power 
to make her heart respond!

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.880
I'll show you, Mercury!

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:13.140
Watch out!

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:28.980
Jeez, that'll happen when you get so rowdy.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.030
Is anybody hurt?

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.990
Neptune-san?

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.300
Did he protect us?

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.020
He's so kind...

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.190
And strong!

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.560
Heart-throbbing infatuation...

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.930
<b>I
n
f
a
t
u
a
t
i
o
n
.
.
.</b>

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:42.560
I lost.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:46.570
True strength is something you 
can show without fighting.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.340
We've still got a long way to go.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:50.870
I've got it!

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.640
A gentle battle where you can 
see strength without fighting.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:57.240
By comparing your muscles!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.820
It's not a verbal or physical fight,

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.880
it's a battle where you just 
show off your leg muscles.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:05.760
A frog that touches your heart with his 
peaceful but macho way of courting!

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:06.820
What do you think?

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.330
God has spoken!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.180
Accepted!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:12.330
<b>Accepted</b>

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.330
<b>Staurois</b>

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:14.150
Thank you, Neptune-san!

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.670
See you, Shimoda-kun!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.210
It's fun to do the simulation yourself.

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:22.620
I like how easy it is to understand.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:30.720
It looks like your approach was accepted.
 Well, for the frog, I mean.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:34.330
Yes, I am glad I was able to help.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:37.530
Right, about your courting methods...

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:44.890
As a show of love, I do want you 
to battle to show off your vigor,

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:48.020
but you saw that it's dangerous 
to fight for real, right?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.950
What should we do?

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:53.440
Since you guys dive in the ocean, 
how about a lung capacity battle?

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:58.000
But I did like Ven-chan's transformation.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.950
Lung capacity and transformation...

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:04.020
Maybe I'll try making them 
inflate when they breathe in?

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:07.640
Sounds good! Would they be like balloons?

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:13.870
Hm, they have ribs around their lungs, 
so they can't inflate their entire body.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.640
What is that?!

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.820
<i>Something</i> got inflated there.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.160
What? Where? What is that?

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.920
Could that be its nose?

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.540
He also inflated it!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:37.720
What did he inflate now?!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.810
Uh, that should be...

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:43.620
The one who shot out that 
red nose lantern won!

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:47.670
The red lantern is the wall of the membrane

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:50.890
that separates the left and right
 sides of the nose.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.810
Th-That's what that is?

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:57.900
I did write that their body inflates, 
but I never imagined it would be that part.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.360
That definitely made something throb...

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.110
Yeah, just hearing that made
 me feel a throb... in my nose.

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.690
God has spoken!

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:07.530
Accepted!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.080
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:09.080
<b>Hooded Seal</b>

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.220
Wait, <i>that</i> kind of throb is fine?

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:13.510
It's okay!

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:18.590
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.740
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:22.930
They're so cute! From here they 
look like a normal seal family.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:25.870
They are the fastest mammal to wean their young.

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:27.890
Seals breastfeed for a whopping four days!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:28.580
So short!

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:30.770
The males look normal at first glance, too,

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:33.780
but when they want to appear stronger,
 they do this!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:34.850
It's black!

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:38.220
What part of the nose is inflating 
to become this black balloon?

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:41.560
That's the skin above the nose.

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.830
They battle with its size and 
the sound of inflating it.

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:47.600
If the opponent doesn't back 
down with this... they do this!

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:50.460
It's red! Doesn't that hurt?

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:54.540
It doesn't hurt! "This redness 
is my determination."

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:57.070
"Do you have what it takes to do this?"

00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:00.000
"If you can't, I'll let 
you off easy. Get out of here."

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.000
All that is what it means!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:05.420
Where does that red balloon come from?

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:07.200
Oh, it's from the nostril, right?

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.900
Yeah, because that's a nasal membrane.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:13.860
By the way, where is your voice coming from?

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:46.530
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
